course: dictionary
lesson: 7159
title: Perhaps and maybe
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Perhaps» means maybe. It tells the reader that something could happen, but nobody is sure. «Venus's whole surface is quite young, perhaps 300 to 700 million years old» shows that scientists have a best guess, not an exact age.
explain: Look at the words around perhaps. A range of numbers, like «300 to 700 million», often comes with it, because the writer can estimate but cannot be exact. In a story, «Perhaps it will rain» means the speaker does not know yet.
explain: Perhaps can also make a request sound polite. «Perhaps you could help me?» is softer than «Help me!», so it is a kind way to ask. The word is doing a different job here, but it still means the speaker is not forcing an answer.
fact: Perhaps means maybe: it could be true, but it is not certain.
fact: Perhaps is an adverb, so it adds information about a verb or a whole sentence.
fact: In science, perhaps shows a guess or a prediction, not a proven fact.
fact: «Perhaps you could help me?» uses perhaps to sound polite.
fact: To check, swap in maybe. If the sentence still makes sense, perhaps is probably the right meaning.
exercise: «Perhaps the bus will be late today.» What does perhaps mean here? | Yesterday | Very quickly | Definitely, for sure | *Maybe, but not certain
exercise: Scientists say Venus is perhaps 300 to 700 million years old. Why do they use perhaps? | *They are not completely sure, so it is a best guess | It is a famous rule | They have measured it exactly | Venus is a shark
exercise: Which sentence uses perhaps to make a request sound polite? | Perhaps it is raining now. | *Perhaps you could pass the salt? | Perhaps the kettle is hot. | Perhaps the dog is asleep.
test: «Perhaps we will finish the game after lunch.» What is the best meaning of perhaps? | *Maybe, we are not sure yet | Never | We will definitely finish | We have already finished
test: Megalodon was perhaps 15 to 20 metres long. Why is the word perhaps useful? | *It shows the length is a sensible guess, not an exact measurement | It shows the length is an exact measurement | It means the shark was a fish called Perhaps | It shows the shark was small
exam: If you swap perhaps for maybe and the sentence still makes sense, what have you learned? | Perhaps is only used in maths | *Perhaps means maybe, so it shows something is not certain | Perhaps always means definitely | Perhaps is a noun for a place
